# Tutorials - Leaflet - a JavaScript library for interactive maps

> Fuente: https://leafletjs.com/examples.html
> Exportado: 2026-07-11 18:52 UTC

## Leaflet Tutorials

Every tutorial here comes with step-by-step code explanation and is easy enough even for beginner JavaScript developers.

---

[![](examples/quick-start/thumbnail.png)](examples/quick-start/)

### [Leaflet Quick Start Guide](examples/quick-start/)

A simple step-by-step guide that will quickly get you started with Leaflet basics, including setting up a Leaflet map (with OpenStreetMap tiles) on your page, working with markers, polylines and popups, and dealing with events.

---

[![](examples/mobile/thumbnail.png)](examples/mobile/)

### [Leaflet on Mobile](examples/mobile/)

In this tutorial, you’ll learn how to create a fullscreen map tuned for mobile devices like iPhone, iPad or Android phones, and how to easily detect and use the current user location.

---

[![](examples/custom-icons/thumbnail.png)](examples/custom-icons/)

### [Markers with Custom Icons](examples/custom-icons/)

In this pretty tutorial, you’ll learn how to easily define your own icons for use by the markers you put on the map.

---

[![](examples/accessibility/thumbnail.png)](examples/accessibility/)

### [Accessible maps](examples/accessibility/)

A guide to basic Leaflet accessibility - make your maps usable to persons of a wide range of abilities.

---

[![](examples/geojson/thumbnail.png)](examples/geojson/)

### [Using GeoJSON with Leaflet](examples/geojson/)

In this tutorial, you’ll learn how to create and interact with map vectors created from [GeoJSON](http://geojson.org/) objects.

---

[![](examples/choropleth/thumbnail.png)](examples/choropleth/)

### [Interactive Choropleth Map](examples/choropleth/)

A case study of creating a colorful interactive [choropleth map](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Choropleth_map) of US States Population Density with GeoJSON and some custom controls. News websites will love this.

---

[![](examples/layers-control/thumbnail.png)](examples/layers-control/)

### [Layer Groups and Layers Control](examples/layers-control/)

A tutorial on how to manage groups of layers and use the layer switching control.

---

[![](examples/zoom-levels/thumbnail.png)](examples/zoom-levels/)

### [Zoom levels](examples/zoom-levels/)

A deeper look into what zoom levels are.

---

[![](examples/crs-simple/thumbnail.png)](examples/crs-simple/crs-simple.html)

### [Non-geographical maps](examples/crs-simple/crs-simple.html)

A primer on `L.CRS.Simple`, how to make maps with no concept of “latitude” or “longitude”.

---

[![](examples/wms/thumbnail.png)](examples/wms/wms.html)

### [WMS and TMS](examples/wms/wms.html)

How to integrate with WMS and TMS services from professional GIS software.

---

[![](examples/map-panes/thumbnail.png)](examples/map-panes/)

### [Working with map panes](examples/map-panes/)

How the default map panes work to display overlays on top of tiles, and how to override that.

---

[![](examples/overlays/thumbnail.gif)](examples/overlays/)

### [Overlays: Image, Video, SVG](examples/overlays/)

Leaflet can help you display images, videos and SVG elements somewhere on the map.

---

